/* ============================================================================
   BBPS biller catalogue - dbo.OperatorMasters and dbo.BBPSConfigurations
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   47_seed_service_and_operator_catalogue.sql seeds a short, GENERIC catalogue so
   a fresh install is not empty: "BSES Rajdhani", "Municipal Corporation", about a
   hundred names an operator recognises. Real BBPS has some four hundred and fifty
   billers, and a client who cannot find theirs in the list cannot sell to them.

   This adds the rest: every biller on the live BBPS catalogue that the generic
   seed does not already cover, in its own service, with the inputs that biller
   actually asks for.

   Two rules make it safe to ship to an existing client:

     * Every biller here is seeded INACTIVE. An operator with no provider behind it
       would otherwise appear in the list and fail at the moment of payment, which
       is worse than not being listed. The provider seed that routes a biller is
       what switches it on - see deploy/optional-seeds/pay1_bbps_biller_routes.sql.

     * Billers the client already has are not touched. The ones that exist under a
       shorter name (MSEDCL (Mahadiscom) = Maharashtra State Electricity Distbn Co
       Ltd) were matched by hand, so this never produces a second row for a biller
       already in the list, and never renames what a client has curated.

   Idempotent, matching on service + operator name, exactly like script 47.
   GENERATED - re-run the generator against a fresh catalogue rather than editing.
   ============================================================================ */

SET NOCOUNT ON;

DECLARE @now datetime2(7) = SYSUTCDATETIME();

